  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that S-sulphocysteine may interact with L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links S-sulphocysteine to Cytochrome c4, which is targeted by a compound called 3-Acetyl-11-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-13-Propanoylilikonapyrone, which in turn targets L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. The second and third pathways show that S-sulphocysteine also targets Fusion glycoprotein F0, which is a target of Mollicelline K and cis-Isopinocamphone, both of which also target L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. These findings indicate that S-sulphocysteine may exert its biological effects through different molecular mechanisms, potentially involving various enzyme targets. The evidence suggests a possible role for S-sulphocysteine in modulating L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction."
